# MIDI source files: the composed background tracks for channel 1.
#
# Declared binary so no line-ending conversion is ever applied to them. Git's own
# NUL-byte sniffing usually gets this right, but a contributor with
# `core.autocrlf=true` and a file whose header happens to look text-like is exactly
# the case where "usually" corrupts a file on checkout, and a corrupted MIDI fails
# at parse time with an error pointing nowhere near the cause.
*.mid binary
*.midi binary

# The bundled datasets. Already stored correctly — git detected them as binary when
# they were committed — but declaring it makes that independent of anyone's config
# rather than dependent on content sniffing.
*.json.gz binary
